  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, the dominant uncertainty is the absolute performance level of this task and the contribution of each design axis. Config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most interpretable RNA-only baseline: PCA is a well-understood linear encoder and singleprofile removes all aggregation/fusion confounds. Establishing this floor is the single most informative first step because (1) it anchors every subsequent comparison—without it, a multimodal or multiprofile result cannot be attributed to a specific design choice; (2) it isolates the RNA signal quality and the task difficulty, which are the two variables that gate all downstream decisions; and (3) it is computationally cheap, preserving budget for the follow-up experiments (image-only baseline, multiprofile aggregation, and multimodal fusion) that will follow logically once the RNA floor is known. No other single experiment reduces as much uncertainty about the most fundamental question: 'how well can RNA alone solve this task with a minimal pipeline?'"
}

